From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mason Morris <masonmorris8@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:55:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Keep a suspended render thread suspended on its new stream

A device follower moves a context from its own thread, so it can move
one whose render thread has answered a suspend before the suspend's
continuation pauses the stream. The render thread's suspended flag
stayed with the old stream, so the new one started Running and played,
and the continuation then paused it under a Running state.

CloseAndRecycle now answers the flag with the graph, and Startup takes
it, so the new render thread starts suspended when the old one was.
---
 src/context/offline.rs |  5 ++++-
 src/context/online.rs  | 16 ++++++++++------
 src/message.rs         |  8 ++++----
 src/render/thread.rs   | 11 ++++++++---
 4 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/context/offline.rs b/src/context/offline.rs
index 6cc9c0e..1ca6460 100644
--- a/src/context/offline.rs
+++ b/src/context/offline.rs
@@ -86,7 +86,10 @@ impl OfflineAudioContext {
 
         let (node_id_producer, node_id_consumer) = llq::Queue::new().split();
         let graph = crate::render::graph::Graph::new(node_id_producer);
-        let message = crate::message::ControlMessage::Startup { graph };
+        let message = crate::message::ControlMessage::Startup {
+            graph,
+            suspended: false,
+        };
         sender.send(message).unwrap();
 
         // track number of frames - synced from render thread to control thread
